  "notes": [
    "The Variations sheet's parallel is committed verbatim as Beckett prints it: \"Golden Mirror Variations Checklist\" (330 rows). This workbook's Master sheet lists no per-parallel names at all (only Base/category + cardNumber/player/team), so stripChecklistSuffix's Master-authority gate never fires, and the Variations sheet has no sibling section to confirm a sheet-wide Checklist-suffix convention either (it is the ONLY section on that sheet). Per convertBeckettChecklistXlsx.cjs's own documented rule (CF-BECKETT-CHECKLIST-IS-A-TITLE-ARTIFACT-NOT-A-NAME), the suffix is left ON rather than guessed off with no corroborating evidence. The sibling 2023 Topps Series 1 file's analogous parallel, correctly stripped, is \"Golden Mirror Image Variation\" -- this may be the same rung under the same naming convention, but it is committed as its own literal string pending a second source or a Master-sheet confirmation, per no-synthetic-parallels.",
    "Removed 4 pure-duplicate rows the source workbook printed for card numbers 371/423/452/505 with unaccented player-name spellings (Livan Soto / Jordan Diaz / Carlos Perez / Jose Miranda) immediately following the plain Base Set run and before the Golden Mirror Variations run began -- each number already carries its correctly-accented row earlier in the same run (Livan Soto / Liván Soto, etc.), identical category/parallel/isAuto/printRun otherwise. Removed as source duplication (CF-A-DUPLICATE-IS-NOT-A-COLLISION), not a second card; measured via planStagedDirectory id-collisions before removal (4 colliding ids, exactly these 4 numbers) and re-verified PASS after."
  ],
